# Kubernetes - Comandos Básicos

## Verificar o cluster

```bash
kubectl cluster-info
```

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

## Aplicar recursos

```bash
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
```

```bash
kubectl apply -f service.yaml
```

```bash
kubectl apply -f .
```

## Listar recursos

### Pods

```bash
kubectl get pods
```

```bash
kubectl get pods -A
```

### Deployments

```bash
kubectl get deployments
```

### Services

```bash
kubectl get services
```

### Namespaces

```bash
kubectl get namespaces
```

## Detalhes dos recursos

```bash
kubectl describe pod <nome-pod>
```

```bash
kubectl describe deployment <nome-deployment>
```

```bash
kubectl describe service <nome-service>
```

## Logs

```bash
kubectl logs <nome-pod>
```

Acompanhar em tempo real:

```bash
kubectl logs -f <nome-pod>
```

Container específico:

```bash
kubectl logs <nome-pod> -c <nome-container>
```

## Acessar um container

```bash
kubectl exec -it <nome-pod> -- sh
```

ou

```bash
kubectl exec -it <nome-pod> -- bash
```

## Escalar deployment

```bash
kubectl scale deployment <nome-deployment> --replicas=3
```

## Reiniciar deployment

```bash
kubectl rollout restart deployment <nome-deployment>
```

## Verificar rollout

```bash
kubectl rollout status deployment <nome-deployment>
```

## Histórico de versões

```bash
kubectl rollout history deployment <nome-deployment>
```

## Rollback

```bash
kubectl rollout undo deployment <nome-deployment>
```

## Expor deployment

```bash
kubectl expose deployment <nome-deployment> --type=LoadBalancer --port=80 --target-port=8080
```

## Port Forward

```bash
kubectl port-forward service/<nome-service> 8080:80
```

ou

```bash
kubectl port-forward pod/<nome-pod> 8080:8080
```

## Remover recursos

```bash
kubectl delete -f deployment.yaml
```

```bash
kubectl delete deployment <nome-deployment>
```

```bash
kubectl delete service <nome-service>
```

```bash
kubectl delete pod <nome-pod>
```

## Monitoramento

```bash
kubectl top pods
```

```bash
kubectl top nodes
```

## Contextos

Ver contextos disponíveis:

```bash
kubectl config get-contexts
```

Ver contexto atual:

```bash
kubectl config current-context
```

Trocar contexto:

```bash
kubectl config use-context <nome-contexto>
```